From d24cdb962770699e76f61efbc2d0ca96a19e3c05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:55:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 156/209] fix: sprite bokeh had no source budget, so a bright
 scene drew a sprite for a tenth of the screen

User: with Scene Referred on and Use Sprite Bokeh on, the number of CoC sources explodes and the
frame rate collapses. Right about the cause, wrong about which parameter: the threshold DID reach
this pass (PostProcessDOF.cpp:117 has run it through ResolveThreshold since S7, and since 3f53d2c4
that means stops over mid grey on the stock path too). What never reached it was the BUDGET.

Root cause. DofBokehRefVS draws one sprite per grid cell whose highlight excess clears the
threshold - 960 x 540 candidate cells at 1080p, culled in the vertex shader and counted nowhere.
A threshold is not a population: "+2 stops over mid grey" is a 90% white in sunlight, the sky, and
every specular, i.e. tens of percent of a physically lit frame, where the old absolute reading
(2.0 engine units = 20 000 cd/m2) picked out light sources only. Each survivor rasterizes a disc
of up to r_DepthOfFieldLensModelSplatMaxCoC (256) native pixels into TWO blended RGBA16F targets:
measured on an 85 mm f/1.4 at 1080p, 10% of the cells is 1 870 Mpx of blending per frame.
decisions/s8-glare-budget.md said the DOF splat was "governed by its own energy split" - true of
where the light goes, silent about how many sprites are drawn. STRUCTURE.md line 432 had already
named this as the outstanding case.

Mechanism (the wave glare's, with the one addition the DOF needs). Four passes in the DOF stage,
before the layer downscale, no CPU round trip:
  DofSpriteWeight       half-res map of (priority, weight, excess) per cell. Priority = the cell's
                        mean excess above the knee x the splat's own fade x the sky weight.
  DofSpriteSourceStats  -> 8x8 tiles (raw, drawn, summed excess, excess handed back)
  DofSpriteStatsReduce  -> a fixed 16x16
  DofSpriteBudget       -> one texel: the cutoff, corrected from last frame's count towards N.
The controller is HDRDiffractionBudgetPS's line for line (multiplicative, asymmetric, dead band,
decay to zero) because it has been measured on this project and its failure modes are written down.

The addition: ONE WEIGHT, TWO CONSUMERS. The excess is read by two passes with different tap
patterns - DownscaleDofPS subtracts it from the gather layers, DofBokehRefVS deposits it - so a
weight computed twice would disagree exactly for the sources on the cutoff and would double count
or drop them. The weight pass writes it once and both scale by the same texel, so the excess a
culled source does not splat is exactly the excess the gather kept. A source that loses its slot
loses its iris SHAPE and keeps its light, spread by the gather - which is what unshaped defocused
light looks like. The glare deposits its losers as a flat one-texel residual instead, because its
layer is additive on top of a complete frame; here the gather layer is what the excess came out of.

A losing cell's quad is collapsed in the vertex shader, so it costs no fill at all. A scene whose
population fits drives the cutoff to 0 and both consumers are then bit-identical to the un-budgeted
pass. Unconditional on both exposure paths (49d61fd0's lesson: the stock path had the same bug);
stock CRYENGINE is untouched because r_DepthOfFieldMode ships as 1 and only a cinecam sets 0.

cvars:
  r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehMaxSources  256, hard cap 4096, 0 = the cap (not "unlimited")
  r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehSkyWeight   0.25 - a far-plane cell competes at this fraction of its
                                       excess. Priority only; the frame's light does not move.
  r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehDebug       1 = the existing silhouette diagnostic (unchanged),
                                       2 = one report a second (population, drawn, cutoff in stops
                                       over the mid grey in force, share handed back to the gather,
                                       sky weight, and the splat's GPU ms), 3 = both.

research/s10-sprite-bokeh-budget.md; decisions/s10-sprite-bokeh-budget.md (5 alternatives, one
chosen); STRUCTURE.md; SpriteBokehSpec.md 7; SceneReferredSpec.md S7; docs/ConsoleReference.md.

