+### r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehMaxSources
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Default | 256 |
+| Purpose | **Source budget** for the hybrid sprite bokeh (`r_DepthOfFieldMode 0` = the camera's **Use Sprite Bokeh**). The splat draws one sprite per grid cell above the highlight threshold, and a threshold does not bound a population: in a physically lit frame "+2 stops over mid grey" is most of a sunlit image, and each of those cells rasterizes a disc of up to `r_DepthOfFieldLensModelSplatMaxCoC` native pixels into two blended fp16 targets. This is the largest number of cells that may draw a shaped disc in one frame. |
+| Who wins a slot | The N brightest, by their excess above the threshold, with SKY de-prioritised — see `r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehSkyWeight`. |
+| Where the rest of the light goes | Back into the **gather**. A cell that cannot afford a disc keeps its excess in the layers the gather is about to blur, so it loses its iris SHAPE and keeps its light, spread the way a lens spreads unshaped defocused light. Nothing darkens when the budget binds, and a one-stop crossfade at the cutoff means nothing pops while panning. |
+| When it does nothing | Whenever the population already fits: the cutoff decays to 0 and both the downscale's energy split and the splat are bit-identical to the un-budgeted pass. In force on both exposure paths (Scene Referred on or off) — the same shader and the same grid run on both. |
+| Hard cap | **4096**, clamped at the consumer, and **0 does not mean unlimited** (0 or less means the cap). A budget whose top end can hang the editor is not a budget — the lesson `r_HDRDiffractionMaxSources` learned on 2026-09-05. A clamped value is said out loud in the debug report rather than swallowed. |
+| Measuring | `r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehDebug 2`. |
+
+### r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehSkyWeight
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Default | 0.25 |
+| Purpose | How hard a **sky** cell competes for `r_DepthOfFieldSpriteBokehMaxSources`. A sky is enormous, sits at infinity so its discs are the largest and most expensive in the frame, and is routinely two to five stops over mid grey; on equal terms it takes every slot and the practicals in the scene lose their bokeh. A cell at the **far plane** enters the energy cutoff with its excess multiplied by this weight. |
+| It is a PRIORITY, not a brightness | Nothing here scales light. A sky cell that **wins** draws its full shaped disc; one that **loses** keeps every bit of its excess in the gather. The frame's total light is identical at every value — only who gets a *shape* changes. |
+| Range | 0 … 1. **1 = sky and scene competing on equal terms.** |
+| Sky test | Linear depth at the far plane (`>= 0.9999`), on all four of the cell's native texels. The same test the wave glare's budget and the camera's metering histogram use. |
 
