+//
+// DofBokehRefVS draws one sprite per grid cell whose highlight excess clears the threshold. A
+// threshold does not bound a population: under a physically lit frame "+2 stops over mid grey" is
+// most of a sunlit image, and each of those cells rasterizes a disc of up to
+// r_DepthOfFieldLensModelSplatMaxCoC native pixels into two blended RGBA16F targets. Measured on
+// an 85 mm f/1.4 at 1080p that is 1 870 Mpx of blending for a tenth of the frame. That is the
+// reported "sprite bokeh on, frame rate gone".
+//
+// Four passes answer, on the GPU with no CPU round trip, the one question the splat needs: what is
+// a source worth this frame, and can it afford a shape?
